        "title": "Status investigator stops chasing weak suspects",
        "summary": "The observability status probes were tuned to reduce noisy investigations and align model evals with real cold-start latency.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Stabilized the marketing StatusView freshness signals and tightened the underlying status policy and probe expectations.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "5a0475f59638f66a335b31a10ea9c92a6e06ee49"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Raised the model-matrix eval timeout to 120s (with warning/outage latency budgets bumped to 180s/360s) so cold model responses no longer trip false outages.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "2049590dd90f5d4c09d19b3cd141daa6d0a52c24"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Constrained the status investigator to evidence-backed commits and paths and dropped weak suspect changes, so RCAs stop citing files and commits that aren't in the evidence packet.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "7c8e0405beda70cdad1e6f405f3c9c168cde63db",
              "7560151f6d3be0c6939c7f288a51398f71186182",
