        "ended_at": "2026-06-16T21:43:05.000Z",
        "title": "Desktop harness reclaims its port and ignores stale env",
        "summary": "The managed local harness sidecar on desktop now detects and replaces stale processes and refuses to trust an inherited managed binary path from a previous install.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Before spawning, the desktop now scans for managed sidecars listening on the harness port and terminates stale ones whose binary no longer matches the bundled path, while leaving the current process untouched.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "d44c39d97f710d17e094f3c793ea6bca937e5af2"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "An inherited AURA_HARNESS_BIN pointing into the managed staging dir is now ignored so the freshly bundled sidecar can be restaged instead of silently reusing an old binary across upgrades.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "7dcb1d58734d26c478b92169a5b866fab3907361"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
